Sure, but it also seems like an intentional choice.  I'd consider
using a tile set that has different tiles for elvenkings and Rodney,
or visible tiles for ghosts (or remapping ghosts to a visible
character), to be circumventing the DevTeam's intent. I'd also say
that both are intentional places where the interface is _not_ intended
to be as simple as possible.

Certainly with ghosts you _could_ far-look at every square with ESP
on, but the choice of character is intended to make such detection
harder even though it's possible within the interface.

It's one reason that I'm generally against using interface patches and
calling it "vanilla"--like most games, Nethack play is partly tied to
how the interface works.  Even colorizing your HP readout affects your
odds of success in real life.  I'm not sure it's a major effect, and I
wouldn't be surprised to see it in future versions, but in real life
people do get careless about checking the status line and it is
slightly easier to win with patches that hold your hand about such
things.



